WEBVTT

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.470
Tohsaka!

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.890
Where do you want me to put these?

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.850
Hold on a sec!

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.860
Can you put all the books together in
one of the corners in the other room?

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.490
Got it!

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.200
Watch out!

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.030
Watch where you're going!

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.910
If you trip on something and break it,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.160
can you imagine what could happen?

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.580
Look at all this.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.380
I'm sure this is all valuable stuff, but still...

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.170
Tohsaka!

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.260
What should I do with this?

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.010
Which one?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.600
Oh, you can leave that one there.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.310
You know, it'd be very dangerous
if that lid opened by mistake.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.020
I-Is that right?

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.190
Okay.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.440
Hey,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.940
can you put this in my room, somewhere near my desk?

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.700
Your room, Tohsaka?

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.620
Um, you don't mind?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:41.870
What are you talking about?

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.750
You know, you don't mind if I go into your room?

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.250
I don't mind if it's you, Shirou.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.630
Oh, and while you're at it,

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.050
please check on Sakura, will you?

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.720
I know she said to carry this up, but...

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.350
Where the heck is Tohsaka's room anyway?

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.730
Tohsaka's house is actually pretty huge.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.520
Oh, Senpai...

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.730
Hey there, Sakura!

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.530
Is Rin almost done?

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:23.490
Not yet. She just asked me to
bring these over to her desk.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.620
Oh, in that case...

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.000
Here you go.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.830
You can put it down here.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.130
Thanks.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.290
That's helpful.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.840
Well, Sakura, how are you doing over here?

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.470
I think I'm making progress,

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.180
but as you can see, there's still so much to do.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.640
To say the least.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.060
So many letters!

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.900
I was just organizing them

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.400
because they were all over the desk.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.660
Let's see... "London, England."

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.990
Is this from the Clock Tower?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.500
Looks like she's been in contact
with them like this for years.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.250
Where does she find the time?

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.630
Rin is amazing after all!

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.300
Tohsaka... She's doing her best.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:25.850
Huh?

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.140
Look at the time.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.560
Shall we go over to Rin?

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:38.980
Rin!

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:40.610
Hey there,

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.360
you two!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.990
I was just about to come get you.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.240
Same here, actually.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.290
What should we do about lunch?

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.130
If I can borrow your kitchen,
I'll be happy to make something.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.500
No, it's fine.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.380
I asked you to help me clean.
I can't ask you to cook for us, too!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.640
I'll be glad to make something.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.720
Um...

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.680
I'll help you!

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.350
Go ahead and use that apron there.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.610
Okay, thank you.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.030
Cat-print...

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.530
<i>Cats...</i>

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.370
<i>I guess she likes cats.</i>

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.040
Oh, nothing.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:44.760
I'm pretty sure we have all the ingredients.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:52.810
Eggs, carrots, leeks, green peppers,
kamaboko, roasted pork.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.890
Yes, that's everything!

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.860
Yeah! Today we're making fried rice!

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.770
Wh-What?

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.570
Excuse me for laughing.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:06.490
I had a feeling you were going
to make something Chinese.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.080
And you know,

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.370
I don't often cook Chinese food,

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.120
so I was hoping you could show me how.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.340
In that case...

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.760
It's not a fancy enough dish to
teach you how to make, but...

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:27.760
Let's get started. Can you help
me chop up the ingredients?

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:28.890
Sure!

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:35.350
Take the roasted pork, carrots,
kamaboko, leeks and green peppers,

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.850
and chop them to the size of the grains of rice.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.070
This is so all the ingredients get cooked
quickly and evenly with a nice texture.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.860
Yes, Chef!

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.000
I'm finished!

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.130
Is something wrong?

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.630
No, no. It's nothing.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.010
So, the next step is...

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.430
<i>I was wondering if I could help,</i>

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.390
<i>but I shouldn't intrude, right?</i>

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:16.850
<i>I should wait quietly.</i>

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:24.270
Okay!

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:30.070
Heat the frying pan and add a little oil.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.540
Cook the carrots over medium heat,
and when they're cooked halfway through,

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:38.000
add the roasted pork, kamaboko and green peppers.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.500
Season it lightly with salt and pepper,

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:43.250
then remove it from the frying
pan and place it onto a plate.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.510
Beat the eggs separately.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.010
Then, add a generous amount of oil into the frying pan

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.010
over medium to high heat, and pour in the beaten eggs.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.850
Scramble them well to make
little pieces of scrambled eggs.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.860
Then, before the eggs are cooked through

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:05.150
add the rice while the eggs are still half-cooked,

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.780
and stir it as if slicing through it with a wooden spatula.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.120
Now, add all the other ingredients
that you've already cooked,

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.700
along with the leeks,

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:18.450
and season it with some Japanese sake, salt and pepper.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.580
When I think of Chinese cooking,

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:24.960
it makes me want to try flipping
the food like they do in restaurants,

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.710
but I'm afraid it will fly all over the place.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.880
Oh that.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.050
But the heat of a household
stovetop isn't strong enough,

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.390
so if you do it too much,

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:37.890
the temperature of the frying pan gets
too low, and the food starts to stick.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:42.480
It's enough to sway the pan back and
forth to mix it without lifting the food.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.650
Fried rice needs to be cooked quickly on high heat!

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:46.940
But...

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.440
this does make it more exciting!

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:59.450
This smell is making me hungry!

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.540
Thanks, I learned a lot from you, Rin!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.130
Let's make a side dish now!

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:15.890
Senpai, thank you for your patience!

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.100
Something smells great!

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:19.970
Did I come back at the right time?

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.230
Yes, perfect timing!

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.360
I thought you'd be sitting back,
relaxing. Where were you?

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.530
I needed to keep myself busy,

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:31.570
so I was cleaning some more.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.910
What's going on?

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.090
This looks so good!

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:51.420
Of course, it does! I made it, after all!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.920
And Sakura helped me.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.760
Please go ahead and enjoy!

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:06.310
This is simple and delicious!

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.610
The rice isn't sticky, but nice and dry.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.030
That's not easy to accomplish!

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.110
But of course!

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:22.410
I don't know if I have the
confidence to make it this good.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.410
But I'd like to make it next time.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:28.170
So please taste it for me, will you, Senpai?

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.420
So now, Sakura is into Chinese cooking, too!

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.380
And...

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:38.220
I'd love to learn more from you, Rin!

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.350
Y-You would?

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:45.640
Yes!

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.770
You're red, Tohsaka.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.780
Shut up, shut up!

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.160
Come on!
